  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is:\n\n**(First number² – Third number) = Second number**\n\n \n• (7, 40, 9) → (7² - 9) = 49 – 9 = **40**.\n \n• (11, 108, 13) → (11² - 13) = 121 – 13 = **108**.\n\nSimilarly, \n\nI. (4, 12, 5) → (4² - 5) = 16 - 5 = 11 **≠** 12.\n\nII. (13, 123, 24) → (13² - 24) = 169 – 24 = 145 **≠** 123.\n\nIII. (9, 67, 10) → (9² - 10) = 81 – 10 = 71 **≠** 67.\n\nIV. (8, 58, 6) → (8² - 6) = 64 – 6 = **58 = 58.** \n\nHence, the correct answer will be** (8, 58, 6).**",
